// endpoint_update_production_mediation.proto — UpdateProductionMediation:
// the production mediator's decisions. AGENT API section. Only a
// repository's standing production mediator
// (repoconfig.v1.LifecycleConfig.production_checks) may call it, through
// `agent-repld production-mediation`.
//
// After each deploy the daemon owes the mediator a CHECK of the span the
// version before it served alone, from the previous landing's finish to this
// landing's start, and briefs it with the log sites new to that span. The
// mediator DECIDES the check: nothing to do, or a set of CHILDREN to dispatch,
// each a one-shot child of the mediator holding findings and the log sites
// they cover, created together and landing at the front of the merge queue.
// Apart from any check, it may FOLD one open child into another when their
// work converges.
//
// THE DAEMON RECORDS WHICH CHILD OWNS WHICH SITE. A site an open child owns is
// left out of every later brief and may not be dispatched again until that
// child lands or closes, so no site is ever worked by two children at once.
//
// Nothing here holds the queue or a deploy: a production check never blocks
// anything.
//
// THE CHECKS CAN BE PAUSED (endpoint_update_production_pause.proto): while
// they are, the mediator is told no span and every action here is refused
// (`paused`).

